meta {
  name: List Bug Reports
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/platform/bug-reports?status=new,triaged,in_progress&limit=50
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

params:query {
  status: new,triaged,in_progress
  limit: 50
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{platformAccessToken}}
}

tests {
  test("returns 200 OK", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });

  test("returns rows, a filtered total and unfiltered status counts", function () {
    const body = res.getBody();
    expect(body.items).to.be.an("array");
    expect(body.total).to.be.a("number");
    expect(body.statusCounts).to.have.property("new");
    expect(body.statusCounts).to.have.property("wont_fix");
  });

  test("includes the report filed in the Bug Reports folder", function () {
    const ids = res.getBody().items.map((item) => item.id);
    expect(ids).to.include(bru.getVar("bugReportId"));
  });

  test("rows carry a derived summary and no screenshot keys", function () {
    const row = res.getBody().items.find(
      (item) => item.id === bru.getVar("bugReportId"),
    );
    expect(row.summary).to.contain("leaderboard");
    expect(row.screenshotCount).to.equal(1);
    // The list is a list: no description, no context, no storage keys.
    expect(row).to.not.have.property("description");
    expect(row).to.not.have.property("screenshots");
  });
}

docs {
  # GET /platform/bug-reports — the Super Admin queue

  Every report on the platform, across every tenant, newest first. Backs
  `/admin/bugs`.

  - **Module:** none (`@SkipModule()`)
  - **Permission:** `platform:bugs:read`
  - **Data scope:** none (`@SkipTenant()`, `@SkipBranch()`) — cross-tenant by
    design; `platform:bugs:read` is the boundary.

  ## Query
  | param    | type   | notes                                                        |
  |----------|--------|--------------------------------------------------------------|
  | status   | csv    | any of `new`,`triaged`,`in_progress`,`resolved`,`wont_fix`. Omit for all. |
  | severity | enum   | `low` \| `normal` \| `high` \| `blocking`                     |
  | agencyId | string | 24-hex                                                        |
  | search   | string | matched against the description via a Mongo **text index**    |
  | limit    | int    | 1–100, default 50                                             |
  | skip     | int    | ≥ 0, default 0                                                |

  `status` is comma-separated so the page's default view — "everything still
  open" — is one request rather than three.

  ## Why `statusCounts` ignores the filters

  They drive the page's filter chips. A count that respected the status filter
  would show `New (12)` only while New was already selected, and every other
  chip at zero. `total` is the filtered count; `statusCounts` is the whole
  collection.

  ## Response `200`
  ```json
  {
    "items": [{
      "id": "68f3…c21",
      "status": "new",
      "severity": "high",
      "summary": "The leaderboard still shows last month's numbers…",
      "reporterName": "Casey Rivera",
      "reporterEmail": "producer@demoagency.local",
      "agencyId": "68a1…f09",
      "agencyName": "Demo Agency",
      "screenshotCount": 1,
      "createdAt": "2026-09-01T14:22:07.113Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-09-01T14:22:07.113Z"
    }],
    "total": 1,
    "statusCounts": { "new": 1, "triaged": 0, "in_progress": 0, "resolved": 0, "wont_fix": 0 }
  }
  ```

  `summary` is the first line of the description, capped at 120 chars and
  derived by `bugReportSummary` in `@sfa/shared` — there is no stored title,
  because one more field to fill in while mid-bug is one more reason not to file.

  `agencyName` is `null` for a report filed by a platform operator, who has no
  agency; the page renders those as "Platform".

  ## Errors
  - `401 Unauthorized` — missing/expired token.
  - `403 Forbidden` — missing `platform:bugs:read` (e.g. any producer).
}
